1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,904
The Application Process.

2
00:00:01,904 --> 00:00:08,009
Before we go further, one distinction
that will save you from setting the wrong

3
00:00:08,009 --> 00:00:13,410
expectations: application and
underwriting are two separate steps. The

4
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:19,281
application verifies the business is real
— that's KYB and KYC. Underwriting

5
00:00:19,281 --> 00:00:25,308
determines terms and limits. A prospect
can be approved on the application and

6
00:00:25,308 --> 00:00:31,022
still not have terms or limits yet. Those
come from the underwriting team.

7
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:36,106
When your prospect clicks the application
link, here's what they'll see — five

8
00:00:36,106 --> 00:00:36,502
steps.

9
00:00:36,502 --> 00:00:38,917
Step one: Qualification.

10
00:00:38,917 --> 00:00:44,638
The first screen asks one question: is
this a US company or an international

11
00:00:44,638 --> 00:00:50,740
company? The prospect selects "I'm a US
company" — the company has a registration

12
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:53,638
number and operates as a legal entity.

13
00:00:53,638 --> 00:00:56,099
Step two: Business details.

14
00:00:56,099 --> 00:01:02,600
This is the longest step — four tabs. The
first tab is company details: legal

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:09,016
business type, legal company name, DBA,
industry, a short description of the

16
00:01:09,016 --> 00:01:14,490
business, incorporation date,
incorporation state, company email,

17
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:20,992
company phone, and EIN. The second tab is
monthly spend — ad spend and non-ad

18
00:01:20,992 --> 00:01:27,578
spend, as dropdown ranges. The third tab
is website address. The fourth tab is

19
00:01:27,578 --> 00:01:29,118
operating address.

20
00:01:29,118 --> 00:01:34,562
Most of this information the prospect has
in front of them. If they have their EIN

21
00:01:34,562 --> 00:01:39,737
and articles of incorporation ready —
which you should have asked them to pull

22
00:01:39,737 --> 00:01:42,493
together — this step takes a few minutes.

23
00:01:42,493 --> 00:01:45,604
Step three: Identity verification.

24
00:01:45,604 --> 00:01:52,023
This is the KYC step. Any beneficial
owner with more than 25% ownership — or,

25
00:01:52,023 --> 00:01:58,358
if no one holds more than 25%, the
controlling officer — clicks "Verify" and

26
00:01:58,358 --> 00:02:04,609
follows the prompts: a photo of their
government-issued ID and a selfie for

27
00:02:04,609 --> 00:02:10,183
biometric verification. This is done
through Plaid and is a federal

28
00:02:10,183 --> 00:02:13,562
requirement, not something unique to us.

29
00:02:13,562 --> 00:02:16,070
Step four: Terms and conditions.

30
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:18,020
Standard legal acceptance.

31
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,528
Step five: Finalize.

32
00:02:20,528 --> 00:02:25,936
This is the final screen, and it has four
items: beneficiaries, controlling

33
00:02:25,936 --> 00:02:31,709
officer, bank account, and documents. The
first two confirm ownership structure.

34
00:02:31,709 --> 00:02:35,436
The bank account connection is where
Plaid comes in.

35
00:02:35,436 --> 00:02:37,665
Bank connection — three paths.

36
00:02:37,665 --> 00:02:43,497
The fastest path: Plaid connects. The
prospect authenticates into their bank

37
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:48,940
through Plaid's OAuth flow, and the
connection verifies instantly. Most

38
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,040
applications go this route.

39
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:56,564
If Plaid doesn't connect — and it happens
— there's a manual path. The prospect

40
00:02:56,564 --> 00:03:02,370
enters their routing and account numbers,
we send a micro-deposit, and they confirm

41
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:06,690
a three-letter code. That takes same-day
to next business day.

42
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:12,000
If the micro-deposit gets blocked — a
bank holiday, for example — the prospect

43
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,171
uploads a recent bank statement directly
in the application. It has to be an

44
00:03:17,171 --> 00:03:22,619
actual statement, not a screenshot. The
partner bank requires the real document.

45
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,873
Documents.

46
00:03:23,873 --> 00:03:29,870
The final item is document upload. For
Net-1, a bank statement may be all that's

47
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:35,259
needed. For float, this is where 24
months of P&L and balance sheets get

48
00:03:35,259 --> 00:03:40,952
attached — but your prospect should
already know that from how you framed it

49
00:03:40,952 --> 00:03:41,939
in discovery.

50
00:03:41,939 --> 00:03:45,004
What happens after they submit.

51
00:03:45,004 --> 00:03:50,284
The application goes to the operations
team for KYB and KYC review. Once

52
00:03:50,284 --> 00:03:55,192
approved, the system creates an
underwriting request — but that's a

53
00:03:55,192 --> 00:04:00,621
separate process covered in the next
module. Application approved does not

54
00:04:00,621 --> 00:04:06,272
mean the prospect has a card yet. It
means the business has been verified and

55
00:04:06,272 --> 00:04:08,875
the deal is ready for underwriting.

56
00:04:08,875 --> 00:04:13,814
That's the full application — five steps,
a few minutes for Net-1, a bit longer if

57
00:04:13,814 --> 00:04:18,692
float documents need to be attached. When
you know what your prospect is going to

58
00:04:18,692 --> 00:04:22,899
see, you can walk them through it with
confidence instead of guessing.
